{
  "protocol": "at",
  "version": "1.2",
  "notes": "Plain text must be the entire body (one trailing newline allowed). JSON name may omit @. Length is 1 to 15 characters: [a-z0-9_], one Extended_Pictographic scalar, a flag pair counted as one character, one non-ASCII currency sign, the Dogecoin sign Ð, one non-ASCII number, or letters from a single non-Latin script (Hiragana, Katakana, and Han are one script). A lone regional indicator, a ZWJ sequence, a keycap, a tag sequence, a combining mark, a mixed script, a whole-script ASCII lookalike, or a skin tone is not a handle. A dot, a DNS marker, or a DX marker never registers a handle. v1.2 adds those characters and does not change any v1.1 canonical handle. v1.1: content type is never consulted; p is compared ASCII case-insensitively and must be 'at' (p:'@' is not a marker); a duplicated JSON key takes its last value.",
